@startuml MODES
' Two maps and two operating modes. members is driven in both, reviews only
' while running: the <<promote>> block is what says where a family moves, so
' reviews is held still in 縮退中. The mode-switching edges are hand-written; the
' frame that keeps every map across them is promotion's to write.
'
' A map is named by the title of its block, not by its PlantUML alias, because
' the alias has to be unique across the diagram. Only one block per map carries
' the !include: a second copy of the same file would collide with the first on
' every state ID and PlantUML would merge the two boxes into one. The other
' parents hold a bodyless block that names the map and nothing else.
!define PROMOTED

state "稼働中" as running {
  running : members ; MemberId ⇸ Member
  running : reviews ; ReviewId ⇸ Review

  state "members : (会員ID : MemberId) ⇸ Member" as runningMembers <<promote>> {
    !include local/MEMBER.puml
  }
  state "reviews : (審査ID : ReviewId) ⇸ Review" as runningReviews <<promote>> {
    !include local/REVIEW.puml
  }
}

state "縮退中" as degraded {
  degraded : members ; MemberId ⇸ Member
  degraded : reviews ; ReviewId ⇸ Review

  state "members : (会員ID : MemberId) ⇸ Member" as degradedMembers <<promote>>
}

[*] --> running

running --> degraded : DEGRADE
degraded --> running : RECOVER

note bottom of runningReviews
  constrain REVIEW_BEGIN?審査ID?会員ID ; $会員ID は $members の定義域にある
end note
@enduml
